---
import { PRICE, REPO_URL, SHIPPED } from "../config";
import Button from "./Button.astro";
import Logo from "./Logo.astro";
---

<section
  id="cta"
  class="wrap relative flex flex-col items-center gap-5 overflow-hidden py-[96px] text-center"
>
  {/* cupertino's geometry and alpha: a wash off the TOP of the plate rather
      than a bleed off the bottom of the page, and .18 rather than .26. It used
      to breathe on a 10s loop; a background that moves competes with the thing
      in front of it, and there is only one thing in front of this. */}
  <div
    class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-[220px]"
    style="background:radial-gradient(50% 100% at 50% 0%,rgb(242 137 92 / 18%),transparent 70%)"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
  </div>

  <Logo size={76} class="relative" />

  <h2
    class="relative m-0 max-w-[19ch] font-display text-[clamp(28px,3.6vw,42px)] leading-[1.1] font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-balance"
  >
    One process. One grant of trust. Read the source.
  </h2>

  <p class="relative m-0 max-w-[52ch] px-5 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.6] text-fg-dim text-pretty">
    A program that holds every credential you own should be readable and compilable by the people
    trusting it. The source is public and stays public; what is sold is the signed build.
  </p>

  {/*
    `SHIPPED` gates the elements that name something you can get. Everything else
    on this page is true whether or not there is a release, which is the rule
    config.ts states: a string outside a SHIPPED branch has to stand on its own.

    Buy points at /buy rather than at Stripe. That path is a redirect the site
    owns, so the checkout URL can move without editing a page — and the app's
    Licence pane links the same one, which matters more, because a URL compiled
    into a shipped binary can never be repointed.
  */}
  <div class="relative flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3 px-5 pt-1.5">
    {
      SHIPPED && (
        <Button href="/download" size="lg">
          Download for macOS
        </Button>
      )
    }
    <Button href={REPO_URL} external variant={SHIPPED ? "secondary" : "primary"} size="lg">
      Read the source <span class="opacity-60">↗</span>
    </Button>
    <code
      class="rounded-[10px] border border-rule-2 px-[22px] py-3 font-mono text-[13px] text-fg-dim"
    >
      make app && make audit
    </code>
  </div>

  {
    SHIPPED ? (
      <p class="relative m-0 text-[12.5px] text-fg-muted">
        {PRICE.price} — {PRICE.covers}. {PRICE.refund}.{" "}
        <a href="/buy" class="text-accent-hi underline underline-offset-2">
          Buy a licence
        </a>{" "}
        ·{" "}
        <a href="/terms" class="underline underline-offset-2">
          terms
        </a>
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p class="relative m-0 text-[12.5px] text-fg-muted">
        {/* The unreachable half of the flag today, and it still has to be true:
            it said the app was code-signed for development only, which stopped
            being the case at 1.0.0. A fallback nobody renders is a fallback
            nobody proofreads. */}
        Between releases — build it from source with <code class="font-mono">make app</code>.
      </p>
    )
  }
</section>
